    "q-132206": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132206",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3})$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=\\sqrt{2},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{t}{t+1}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}}⟩.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3}⟩,$ since the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3})$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{\\frac{t}{t+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}(t+1)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{2(t+1)^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}(1+1)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{1}{2(1+1)^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2(2)^{3/2}},-\\frac{1}{2(2)^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3}⟩+4\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3}⟩+4⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{2}{3}⟩+⟨4,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{10}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
