    "q-35114": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35114",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ for the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t),$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and ${r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨0,\\,-2,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the radius of the osculating circle at  $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=\\frac{{2}^{3}}{\\,2\\,}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
